General lemmas from the Lean package of Alpöge and Buckmaster

Forty-two modules of PDE/Analysis hold general lemmas, with their proofs, from the Lean package of
Levent Alpöge and Tristan Buckmaster for their paper "Finite-time blow-up for the Navier–Stokes
equations" (https://github.com/tristanbuckmaster/navier-stokes, folder lean/, commit ad53419). That
repository has no license file; the modules are included with the permission of the authors. The
lemmas came here from BlowupZoo (https://github.com/lean-dojo/BlowupZoo), which includes the
package with the permission of the authors (20 November 2026) and held these lemmas in its folder
AtlasCandidates/ until they moved here. Each of these modules names the authors in its header. The
statement of each lemma names only objects of Mathlib and nine definitions of the same modules: no
profile, no certificate and no other object of the paper's construction. The proofs come from the
authors' proofs as they stood in BlowupZoo, with the changes that the rest of this paragraph
lists. BlowupZoo ported them to Lean v4.36.0 and proved some in one line from a theorem of
Mathlib, of this library or of the same module; its NavierStokes/Unforced/PORTING.md records each
step. The move changed proofs where the options and linters of this library required it, and it
changed statements and names. Against BlowupZoo:
166 lemmas have another name (162 got a name that says what they state, 4 had a name that was
taken); 22 hypotheses that no proof needs left 18 statements; 7 lemmas take weaker instance
arguments; 27 lemmas were removed (25 because another lemma of these modules states the same
or more, two because a theorem of this library does: one of the two, hasDerivAt_sq, was a
private lemma of this library, with its proof, before these modules came, and is public now in
PDE/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/Square.lean); 59 lemmas are now proved
in a few lines from another statement (50 from a lemma of these modules, 2 from an older theorem
of this library, 7 from a theorem of Mathlib); 5 lemmas were stated more generally; two general
lemmas, hasDerivAt_eval_mvPolynomial and setIntegral_mul_comp_eq_sum_triPoly, were added, each
with the authors' proof of a pair of its cases; and one lemma,
aestronglyMeasurable_pi_pi_of_forall, is new and not from the package. The layout of the
statements and the lambda arrow follow this library, and each module opens its namespaces once,
after the imports. The names of the lemmas that were proved next to one use, the docstrings and
the module documentation were written for BlowupZoo and for this repository.

